      "content": "They often point to early 20th-century intelligence testing data, claiming these standardized scores reflect innate differences. Some proponents reference concepts like genetic determinism, suggesting that heritability estimates for intelligence are high enough to account for group differences. They might also cite specific, often contested, studies that attempt to link genetic markers or ancestry to cognitive performance. These arguments rely heavily on selective interpretation of statistical correlations found in historical data.",
